#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Downloads LEGO part thumbnail images for every element ID used in your
MOC parts inventory, and saves them into an "images" folder next to this
script. Uses only the Python standard library, so no pip install needed.

USAGE:
    python3 download_part_images.py

Then take the "images" folder this creates and put it in your GitHub repo
right next to index.html (same folder level). Commit and push (or drag
both into the GitHub web UI). Once live, the app will automatically load
thumbnails from your own site first, before ever trying LEGO's CDN or a
browser cache -- so images work for every visitor, instantly, with no
CORS proxy and no per-browser storage limits.

For repos with thousands of parts, GitHub web uploads cap out around 100
files per batch, which gets tedious fast. Run this script from inside a
local git clone of your repo instead, and it will offer to add, commit,
and push every image in one shot when it finishes -- no batching, no
tracking which files you already uploaded.

Re-running this script later only downloads files that are missing, so
it's safe to run again after adding new parts to your inventory.

Generated from your inventory on 2026-09-08 (2106 element IDs).
"""

